    "vacancy": "45 posts total: Steno Typist 15; Clerk 20; Storekeeper 10. Post counts are from official Advertisement No. 03/2026.",
    "qualification": "Steno Typist: Bachelor's degree from a recognized university; at least 120-hour computer course with hands-on experience in personal computer/office productivity/desktop publishing from a government-recognized or ISO-9001-certified reputed institution, OR DOEACC 'O' Level-equivalent course; Punjabi matriculation from a recognized board (as first/second/additional language or accepted equivalent) by the application deadline. Clerk: same degree, computer and Punjabi requirements. Storekeeper: Bachelor's degree with Economics, B.Com. or B.B.A.; same computer and Punjabi requirements. Read each post's official eligibility PDF for full conditions.",
    "age": "Age as on 01/01/2026: minimum 18 years; General-category maximum 37 years. Punjab government/university rules apply to other categories and eligible special categories.",
    "fee": "Non-refundable, online only: SC and PwD candidates ₹590; all other candidates ₹1,180 (including GST), for each post applied to. A separate application and fee is required for each post, where applicable.",
    "selection": "Post-wise process from official eligibility PDFs: All posts require a qualifying Matric-level Punjabi language test (50% minimum; 60 minutes; no negative marking; not counted toward merit). Clerk: main exam 100 MCQs/100 marks/100 minutes, 40% qualifying, 0.25 negative mark per wrong answer; then qualifying Punjabi and English typing tests, each 10 minutes, minimum 30 WPM in both languages, max 8% errors; final merit from main exam. Steno Typist: main exam 100 MCQs/100 marks/100 minutes, minimum 40%, 0.25 negative mark per wrong answer; then English and Punjabi shorthand tests (dictation 80 WPM, transcription 15 WPM, max 8% errors in each); merit weightage main exam 30%, English shorthand 35%, Punjabi shorthand 35%. Storekeeper: main exam 100 MCQs/100 marks/100 minutes with Part A general topics 30 marks and Part B core subject 70 marks; minimum 40% separately in both parts, 0.25 negative mark per wrong answer; merit from main exam marks. Document scrutiny/verification follows as prescribed.",
    "documents": "For the relevant post, prepare: recent photograph and signature; proof of date of birth/Matric certificate; degree and marksheets; computer course certificate or DOEACC 'O' Level-equivalent proof; Punjabi matriculation certificate; Storekeeper applicants' degree showing Economics/B.Com./B.B.A.; valid Punjab residence/domicile certificate (the general instructions say the residence certificate for reservation claims must not be older than 5 years on the online closing date); SC/BC/PwD/Ex-servicemen or other applicable relaxation certificates; and in-service NOC/forwarding through proper channel where applicable. The notice also requires a prescribed offline application form plus printout of the finally submitted online application and supporting documents. Offline form deadline for non-in-service applicants: 16/10/2026 04:00 PM; in-service hard-copy/forwarded application deadline: 21/10/2026 04:00 PM. Follow the official instructions and individual post checklist.",
